# Expanding Kali Linux Disk Space Using GParted

## Overview

This project documents how I expanded the root partition of a Kali Linux virtual machine running in VirtualBox after the system reached 100% disk usage. Instead of deleting files or reinstalling the operating system, I used GParted Live to reorganize the partition layout and extend the root partition safely.

## Objective

- Identify the cause of the storage issue.
- Expand the Kali Linux root partition.
- Preserve all existing files and system configurations.
- Verify the new partition size after the resize.

## Tools Used

- Kali Linux
- Oracle VirtualBox
- GParted Live
- Linux Terminal

## Commands Used

```bash
df -h
lsblk
```

## Result

The root partition was successfully expanded from **38 GB** to **59 GB**, increasing the available free space to approximately **18 GB** without reinstalling Kali Linux or losing any data.

